From: Athena NSS maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: nss: reset dropped total for each peer statistics entry

tx_dropped is initialized once before the peer loop. Later peers receive
the sum of their own drops and all preceding peers' drops in the message.
Reset the temporary immediately before summing the current peer's bins.
This changes statistics accounting only. It does not change TX scheduling,
TID classification, WMM, firmware settings or packet handling.

Candidate for firmware source 90448eeb2b8f5d172caedfe6d96ab3bacb058c09
after its mac80211 patch sequence. Not installed or submitted upstream.
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -188,6 +188,7 @@ static void ath11k_nss_get_peer_stats(struct ath11k_base *ab, struct nss_wifili_peer_stats *stats)
 		peer->nss.nss_stats->tx_bytes += tx_bytes;
 		peer->nss.nss_stats->tx_retries += pstats->tx.retries;
 
+		tx_dropped = 0;
 		for (j = 0; j < NSS_WIFILI_TQM_RR_MAX; j++)
 			tx_dropped += pstats->tx.dropped.drop_stats[j];
 
